17","site":"T Nation · 200 posts · 2005"},{"title":"Hunting for Beginners","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/hunting-for-beginners/196025","site":"T Nation · 185 posts · 2013"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Bear's grease hair pomade — Grokipedia","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Bear's_grease"},{"title":"Bear grease - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_grease"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Hair (scalp)","chain":["Apply scented fat dressing","Hair coated, shiny and styleable","Claimed hair growth"],"effect":"claimed","text":"Users applied it for shine and hold; marketers claimed it regrew hair. Gloss was the plainly visible effect."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Bear's_grease","lead":["Bear's grease is the rendered fat of bears, used as a hair pomade in Europe and by many Native American groups. It was long marketed as a baldness remedy on the idea that bears' thick coats would transfer to people.[1]","Writers including Dioscorides in the first century and Nicholas Culpeper in 1653 recommended it for hair loss.[1] Atkinsons of London became the best-known seller, with a chained-bear logo, and kept it in production until after World War I.[1] As demand outstripped supply, makers substituted pig fat, suet and lard, scented with lavender, thyme or rose; one 1850s estimate held that about 99 percent of English \"bear grease\" contained pig fat.[1]","Among the Sauk, Huron and Delaware, men and women applied bear grease daily to make hair shinier.[1]"],"infobox":[["Type","Rendered animal-fat pomade"],["Best-known brand","Atkinsons of London"],["Era","Antiquity to about World War I"]],"sections":[{"h":"History","paras":["Bear fat was a popular remedy for male hair loss from at least about 70 CE until about World War I.[1] Dioscorides described rendering the fat by washing, melting and straining.[1] Grokipedia adds that a London apothecary named Townsend is credited with an early 17th-century product, though this account is less certain.[2]","George Cruikshank's 1823 cartoon alludes to Russian bear grease, then considered the best.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1653","event":"Culpeper writes that bear fat stops hair falling out.[1]"},{"year":"1823","event":"Cruikshank cartoon references Russian bear grease.[1]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Bear grease","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_grease","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Bear's grease","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Bear's_grease","source":"Grokipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Flame Free Confession III: Even More Flame Free (Part 1)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/flame-free-confession-iii-even-more-flame-free-part-1/264067","site":"T Nation · 10000 posts · 2020"},{"title":"More Trouble Than I Am Worth: Chaos Is The Plan (T3hPwnisher Log)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/more-trouble-than-i-am-worth-chaos-is-the-plan-t3hpwnisher-log/276232","site":"T Nation · 8677 posts · 2021"},{"title":"Rising From the Ashes (CL)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/rising-from-the-ashes-cl/233718","site":"T Nation · 6788 posts · 2017"},{"title":"Things That Make You Chuckle","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/things-that-make-you-chuckle/240079","site":"T Nation · 6256 posts · 2018"},{"title":"Titan Tim Tackling his Twenties","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/titan-tim-tackling-his-twenties/254087","site":"T Nation · 4707 posts · 2019"},{"title":"Atlas13 Burning the Boats","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/atlas13-burning-the-boats/259312","site":"T Nation · 3716 posts · 2019"}]}